No upstream pull request is opened yet.

The interface monitor must announce addresses that predate its startup.
See docs/features/interfaces.md, "Monitoring".

AddrSubscribeWithOptions with ListExisting sends RTM_GETADDR on a socket
subscribed to the IPv4 and IPv6 address multicast groups. NetlinkSocket.Send
used the bound sockaddr as the destination, so the request was also sent to
those groups. Sending multicast requires CAP_NET_ADMIN: a read-only daemon
therefore failed at startup with EPERM. Requests belong to the kernel's
unicast address; the socket's subscribed groups remain unchanged for receiving
notifications. TestAddressSubscriptionDumpsWithoutNetAdmin checks the dump
with CAP_NET_ADMIN removed from the calling thread.

